    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 3 tests run, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied on owner creation.\n\n**New file \u2014 `util/AddressNormalizer.java`:** a pure-function utility mirroring the existing `TelephoneNormalizer`/`HouseholdNormalizer`. Its `normalize(String)`:\n- trims and collapses whitespace runs to a single space,\n- upper-cases,\n- expands whole-word street abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). Expansion is per whole word, so `ST` embedded in e.g. `EAST` is left alone.\n- A blank/whitespace-only address reduces to the empty string.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:** added a `normalizeAddress(...)` step at the very start of `addOwner`, before `rejectBlankOwnerFields`. It writes the normalized address back onto the request DTO (leaving a null address untouched so it's still reported as missing). Because the normalized value is written back to the DTO:\n- **Required-field check** now sees the post-normalization address, so a value blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n- **Household duplicate detection** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`) and the **shared household id** (`toHouseholdId`) both read `getAddress()`, so they now operate on the normalized form.\n- The stored and returned `address` is the normalized value.\n\nThis matches the three acceptance tests: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and `\"   \"` \u2192 400.\n\nOne behavioral note worth flagging: `updateOwner` was left unchanged \u2014 the spec scopes normalization to when an owner is *created*, and no test covers update, so I didn't broaden the change there. If you'd like update to normalize too for consistency, I can extend it.",
